186421464 1083 #uuid "03305bbd-2ed9-5a18-8c72-9c0d0c631c78" 13194139534433 17592186045417 true] [17592186421465 1080 "28" 13194139534433 17592186045417 true] [17592186421465 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139534433 17592186045417 true] [17592186421465 1083 #uuid "78c29a36-9fe5-5900-be19-eb34c038c994" 13194139534433 17592186045417 true] [17592186421466 1080 "36" 13194139534433 17592186045417 true] [17592186421466 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139534433 17592186045417 true] [17592186421466 1083 #uuid "97e1e9e0-3fe5-5a2d-b26c-2e7b570ac0c3" 13194139534433 17592186045417 true] [17592186421467 1080 "16" 13194139534433 17592186045417 true] [17592186421467 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139534433 17592186045417 true] [17592186421467 1083 #uuid "e135fd94-1acc-52d5-ad78-5d64f964e29a" 13194139534433 17592186045417 true] [17592186421468 1080 "32" 13194139534433 17592186045417 true] [17592186421468 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139534433 17592186045417 true] [17592186421468 1083 #uuid "e888d5f3-7dc6-5267-ad8c-2c21bc41dcbd" 13194139534433 17592186045417 true] [17592186421469 1075 #edb/ref 17592186421464 13194139534433 17592186045417 true] [17592186421469 1075 #edb/ref 17592186421465 13194139534433 17592186045417 true] [17592186421469 1075 #edb/ref 17592186421466 13194139534433 17592186045417 true] [17592186421469 1075 #edb/ref 17592186421467 13194139534433 17592186045417 true] [17592186421469 1075 #edb/ref 17592186421468 13194139534433 17592186045417 true] [17592186421469 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139534433 17592186045417 true] [17592186421469 1077 "selection" 13194139534433 17592186045417 true] [17592186421469 1078 #edb/ref 17592186421467 13194139534433 17592186045417 true] [17592186421469 1079 #uuid "600bf7ec-a1e3-56fd-89d4-4751fb47440c" 13194139534433 17592186045417 true] [17592186421470 1068 #edb/ref 17592186421469 13194139534433 17592186045417 true] [17592186421470 1069 "q-226134" 13194139534433 17592186045417 true] [17592186421470 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534433 17592186045417 true] [17592186421470 1071 "![](images/95/958965484cd271c5eb7ccfc8bf913386e57b9b733719885d232e562063969ca8.png)\n\nConsider the vector field $F=-x\\,i+2y\\,j$ and a square $C$ with side length $4$ centered at $O,$ as shown above. Calculate the flux of $F$ across $C.$\n\n*Hint: You may use the fact that, due to symmetry, the flux is equal across the vertical sides, and similarly for the horizontal sides.*" 13194139534433 17592186045417 true] [17592186421470 1072 #uuid "f9f7d0a1-c461-5247-ab30-95b875686e93" 13194139534433 17592186045417 true] [17592186421470 1074 "If $F$ is a vector field and $C$ is a piecewise-smooth, simple, closed curve, then the flux of $F$ across $C$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∮}_{C}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}s,\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ denotes the outward-pointing unit normal vector to $C.$ In this case, we have\n\n$$\n{∮}_{C}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}s={\\int }_{{C}_{1}}F\\cdot {n}_{1}\\,\\text{d}s+{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}F\\cdot {n}_{2}\\,\\text{d}s+{\\int }_{{C}_{3}}F\\cdot {n}_{3}\\,\\text{d}s+{\\int }_{{C}_{4}}F\\cdot {n}_{4}\\,\\text{d}s,\n$$\n\nwhere the sides ${C}_{i}$ and unit vectors ${n}_{i}$ are shown below.\n\n![](images/3b/3bd953b7fb02b90a55a29bea6f58ff9bd8bab77d62b1df1c547ca899656d37a3.png)\n\nWe compute this integral in two stages. \n\n- First, consider the side ${C}_{1}.$ We have that ${n}_{1}=i,$ and therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{{C}_{1}}F\\cdot {n}_{1}\\,\\text{d}s & ={\\int }_{{C}_{1}}(-x\\,i+2y\\,j)\\cdot i\\,\\text{d}s \\\\  & =-{\\int }_{{C}_{1}}x\\,\\text{d}s.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis is a line integral with respect to arc length, which we can evaluate in the usual way. Parameterizing the side ${C}_{1},$ we have\n\n$$\nr(t)=2\\,i+t\\,j,\\,⇒\\,{r}^{′}(t)=j,\\,t\\in [-2,2].\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-{\\int }_{{C}_{1}}x\\,\\text{d}s & =-{\\int }_{-2}^{2}2\\cdot ||{r}^{′}(t)||\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =-2{\\int }_{-2}^{2}\\text{d}t \\\\  & =-2\\cdot 4 \\\\  & =-8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nBy symmetry, the flux integral across the side ${C}_{3}$ must be the same. Therefore,\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{{C}_{1}}F\\cdot {n}_{1}\\,\\text{d}s={\\int }_{{C}_{3}}F\\cdot {n}_{3}\\,\\text{d}s=-8.\n$$\n\n- Next, we consider the side ${C}_{2}.$ We have that ${n}_{2}=j,$ and therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}F\\cdot {n}_{2}\\,\\text{d}s & ={\\int }_{{C}_{2}}(-x\\,i+2y\\,j)\\cdot j\\,\\text{d}s \\\\  & =2{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}y\\,\\text{d}s.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis is a line integral with respect to arc length, which we can evaluate in the usual way. Parameterizing the side ${C}_{2},$ we have\n\n$$\nr(t)=t\\,i+2\\,j,\\,⇒\\,{r}^{′}(t)=i,\\,t\\in [-2,2].\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}y\\,\\text{d}s & =2{\\int }_{-2}^{2}2\\cdot ||{r}^{′}(t)||\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =4{\\int }_{-2}^{2}\\text{d}t \\\\  & =4\\cdot 4 \\\\  & =16.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nBy symmetry, the flux integral across the side ${C}_{4}$ must be the same. Therefore,\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}F\\cdot {n}_{2}\\,\\text{d}s={\\int }_{{C}_{4}}F\\cdot {n}_{4}\\,\\text{d}s=16.\n$$\n\nFinally, then\n\n$$\n{∮}_{C}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}s=2\\cdot (-8)+2\\cdot 16=16.\n$$" 13194139534433 17592186045417 true]] :edb/tempids {"answer-03305bbd-2ed9-5a18-8c72-9c0d0c631c78" 17592186421464 "answer-78c29a36-9fe5-5900-be19-eb34c038c994" 17592186421465 "answer-97e1e9e0-3fe5-5a2d-b26c-2e7b570ac0c3" 17592186421466 "answer-e135fd94-1acc-52d5-ad78-5d64f964e29a" 17592186421467 "answer-e888d5f3-7dc6-5267-ad8c-2c21bc41dcbd" 17592186421468 "answer-field-600bf7ec-a1e3-56fd-89d4-4751fb47440c" 17592186421469 "question-f9f7d0a1-c461-5247-ab30-95b875686e93" 17592186421470} :edb/committed false :edb/speculative true}
